# Protected paths (space.yaml `protected:`, rules.md section 8, gate.MINIMUM_PROTECTED and
# gate.ANY_DEPTH). In a space, pull requests touching these wait for the owner's one click and
# everything else lands on green; an approved template release lands on green too. `onboard`
# replaces @OWNER-LOGIN with the owner's GitHub login and keeps this list in step with space.yaml.
# The file names who decides; the gate's verdict enforces it. A space turns on no code-owner
# review: a release pull request is opened with the owner's own token, and GitHub never lets the
# author approve, so every release would stop (SECURITY.md). In the template repository pull
# requests land on green, machinery included, and the release tag is the human gate; a template
# with a second maintainer may require a code owner's review there.

